maluos-memory (0.1.0) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Phase 13 slice 4 (docs/phase13-slice4-memory.md): the memory face of a
    MaluOS host. A Unix socket for local principals (recall, remember,
    forget, usage, the facts the heartbeat carries) and an overlay listener
    for the estate (a slice 2 envelope as the credential, verified against
    the peers the office publishes; the delegated scopes intersected with
    what this host shares; claims, never records). `maluctl memory`: status,
    facts, whoami, recall [--estate], remember, forget, usage, share,
    unshare, expose, unexpose, keys, sync, reload. The first-boot component
    makes the role, the guest and sync principals and the configuration.

 -- Edward Honour <ed@maludb.org>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:00:00 +0000
